<title>FRANCE: Schiphol top EU cargo growth airport in May.</title>
<headline>Schiphol top EU cargo growth airport in May.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amsterdam Schiphol airport recorded the highest percentage gain in cargo traffic in May 1997 compared to the same month last year of the EU's top cargo-handling airports, Paris airport authority (ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>The three London airports combined recorded the highest growth for the period January-May 1997.</p>
<p>Following are the relevant ADP figures, in tonnes:</p>
<p>    Airport	    May 97	  May 96</p>
<p>    London*	   128,929	  up  6.9 percent</p>
<p>    Frankfurt	 107,668	down  0.1</p>
<p>    Amsterdam	  97,330	  up 12.4</p>
<p>    Paris**	    91,012	  up  4.2</p>
<p>    Airport	 Jan-May 97	Jan-May 96</p>
<p>    London*	   619,308	  up  7.6 percent</p>
<p>    Frankfurt	 547,781	  up  3.0</p>
<p>    Amsterdam	 473,163	  up  6.3</p>
<p>    Paris**	   456,716	  up  2.9</p>
<p>*includes Heathrow, Gatwick and Stansted.</p>
<p>**includes Charles de Gaulle and Orly.</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
